// QBZ — Steam Deck (neptune) controller layout, seeded by qbz-add-to-steam.
//
// Based on the stock Steam "Gamepad" template (controller_neptune_gamepad_joystick.vdf,
// Steam client 2026-06) — PURE GAMEPAD: only virtual X360 pad output, NO keyboard
// or mouse emulation, so QBZ's own gilrs gamepad thread is the single input source
// (see qbz-nix-docs/steam-deck/STEAM_DECK_GAME_MODE_PLAN.md, PR 3/PR 5).
//
// The one deviation from the template: Y is bound to Steam's "Show Keyboard"
// system action (controller_action SHOW_KEYBOARD — token verified in
// steamclient.so) as a manual OSK fallback next to the steam://open/keyboard
// deeplink. Y therefore does NOT emit an XInput button.
//
// TODO(verify-on-hardware): this file is authored from the known exported
// config format, not yet exported/validated by the Deck UI. Do the one-time
// validation from the plan: load it on a real Deck in Game Mode, confirm the
// layout applies on first launch (configset_<serial>.vdf path) and that Y
// opens the OSK, then re-export and replace this file if the format drifted.
"controller_mappings"
{
	"version"		"3"
	"title"		"QBZ Kiosk (gamepad + Y=keyboard)"
	"description"		"Pure gamepad layout for the QBZ kiosk: D-pad/stick navigate, A activates, B goes back, Y shows the Steam keyboard. No keyboard/mouse emulation."
	"controller_type"		"controller_neptune"
	"major_revision"		"0"
	"minor_revision"		"0"
